see "../src/harness.vox".

(A2 follow-up (plan 322, steer): repro.sh is generated text, not a shell
 command vox-fuzz itself runs, but it still splices vox_binary into a
 shell script for someone else to run later. Before this, that splice
 was raw - a --vox path containing a space produced a repro.sh broken
 for whoever ran it, the same benign-corruption shape as finding 02, one
 step removed. Force an ICE finding through a --vox path with a space in
 it and confirm the generated repro.sh both names that path correctly
 and actually runs. Run from the repo root, where ./build/vox-fuzz lives
 after `make build`.)

a number called 'the cleanup before' is 'run shell' of "rm -rf './vf repro shim' ./vf_repro_findings ./vf_repro_output.txt" and 5000.
a number called 'the shim directory' is 'run shell' of "mkdir -p './vf repro shim'" and 5000.
a number called 'the shim body' is 'run shell' of "printf '#!/bin/sh\necho \"thread .main. panicked\" >&2\nexit 101\n' > './vf repro shim/voxpanic'" and 5000.
a number called 'the shim permission' is 'run shell' of "chmod +x './vf repro shim/voxpanic'" and 5000.

a list called 'the fuzz arguments' is ["gen", "--seed", "950", "--count", "1", "--budget", "4", "--timeout", "3000", "--vox", "./vf repro shim/voxpanic", "--out", "./vf_repro_findings"].
a text called 'the fuzz verdict' is supervise of "./build/vox-fuzz" and 'the fuzz arguments' and 30000.

a number called 'the repro run' is 'run shell' of "./vf_repro_findings/ice/950/repro.sh > ./vf_repro_output.txt 2>&1" and 10000.
a number called 'the repro check' is 'run shell' of "grep -q 'exit: 101' ./vf_repro_output.txt" and 5000.
Print "repro.sh ran the shimmed compiler: {'the repro check' is 0}".

